  "weather": {
    "summary": "Early October in Columbia averages an 80°F afternoon high and a 63°F morning low. Ten-year observed range for these dates: 68°F to 97°F highs, 48°F to 77°F lows. Measurable rain on about 1 day in 5, but the shoulder-season swings are real.",
    "details": "This is a two-wardrobe weekend. Mornings at the first game are genuinely cool — bring a jacket. Afternoons can still reach the mid-90s, so bring the full heat kit as well: water, electrolytes, sunscreen, cooling towels. Rain is unlikely on any single day, though not impossible. Start hydrating the day before travel. Recomputed September 18, 2026 from ten years of recorded daily observations for Columbia, SC (2016–2025, Open-Meteo historical archive). A reliable daily forecast becomes available around September 28–30.",
